    short_description: 'SAFETY-HEAVY entry alongside Ashwagandha and Curcumin. The best-evidenced oestrogen-free botanical for hot flushes and night sweats - which is a lower bar than it sounds. Contested evidence at the highest level (IMS 2025 grants moderate certainty; NAMS 2023 says insufficient and does NOT recommend; Cochrane null on flush frequency). LiverTox Likelihood Score A (highest) - rare but real and unpredictable idiosyncratic hepatotoxicity. Second-line option for peri/postmenopausal women who cannot or will not use MHT and have already explored prescription non-hormonal options. Coach never initiates - every tier begins at the GP.',
    what_it_does: 'Dried rhizome and root of Actaea racemosa (syn. Cimicifuga racemosa), Ranunculaceae, native to eastern North America. Chemistry poorly resolved - over 100 identified constituents (>40 triterpene glycosides, >20 polyphenols, >70 nitrogenous compounds); the actives are unknown, and "standardised to triterpene glycosides" is a partial control at best. NOT a classical oestrogen - ovariectomised-rat assays negative for uterotrophic and vaginal-cornification effects; human trial data show hormone levels + endometrial thickness + breast density unchanged. Best current mechanistic guess is serotonergic (5-HT7 receptor binding + N-omega-methylserotonin candidate active + 5-HT1A/mu-opioid/dopaminergic/GABAergic in vitro activity), which is biologically coherent for a vasomotor effect via hypothalamic thermoregulation without hormonal action - but EMA position remains "neither the mode of action nor the constituents relevant for the improvement of menopausal complaints are known." Efficacy is genuinely contested at the highest level: HALT trial (Newton 2006 n=351) and Cochrane 2012 (Leach & Moore CD007244) both found no separation from placebo on flush frequency; NAMS 2023 rates insufficient evidence and does NOT recommend. Positive column: Franco 2016 JAMA NMA, Schellenberg 2012 Ze 450 dose-ranging (manufacturer-funded), Castelo-Branco 2021 iCR meta-analysis (heavily industry-affiliated), and IMS 2025 systematic review (search Jan 2022-Dec 2024, 158 studies, GRADE - grants moderate-certainty support for menopausal/vasomotor symptoms, one of only 5 interventions to reach moderate/high certainty; but explicitly NOT for anxiety or depression). Extract identity is the recommendation - three EMA-recognised preparations: iCR (isopropanolic, Remifemin), Ze 450 (ethanolic, Femular/Femular Forte), and BNO 1055 (ethanolic, Klimadynon/Menofem). Effect is modest vs MHT (~70-80% VMS reduction) or fezolinetant (~63% vs 40% placebo).',
