    what_it_does: 'Extracellular (blood) buffering agent - works OUTSIDE the muscle, unlike beta-alanine which works inside. Ingestion raises blood [HCO3-] and blood pH producing induced metabolic alkalosis. Conventional threshold rise >=5 mmol/L (some sources >=4) but this is a heuristic NOT a validated threshold - trials with only +2.8 to +3.7 mmol/L rises (enteric-coated, hydrogel) have produced clear performance improvements, so do NOT tell an athlete a smaller rise means the dose "failed." Elevated extracellular buffering steepens the H+ and lactate- gradient across the sarcolemma during high-intensity exercise, accelerating H+ efflux via monocarboxylate transporters MCT1/MCT4 and defending intramuscular pH for longer. Delays acidosis-driven impairment of glycolytic enzyme activity, Ca2+ handling, and actin-myosin cross-bridge formation. Secondary mechanism via strong ion difference (SID) - lowered interstitial K+, increased K+ efflux, enhanced post-exercise K+ reuptake indicating increased Na+/K+-ATPase activity; preserves sarcolemmal and T-tubular excitability independent of pH buffering. AIS Framework Group A alongside caffeine, beta-alanine, dietary nitrate, creatine, glycerol. **BUT Group A does NOT mean large effect or high certainty** - AIS Group A is a statement about evidence supporting use in a defined situation, not about effect magnitude or GRADE certainty (which is LOW to MODERATE throughout). Effect window ISSN 30 s to 12 min; AIS good evidence 1-7 min; meta-analyses cluster 1-10 min; recent data support 16.1 km TT +2.1% (fasted, enteric-coated), 40 km TT +1.42% (hydrogel, Shannon 2024 12/14 improved), 4 km TT in 30 degrees C heat +1.6%. Best-evidenced by endpoint (Grgic 2021 umbrella): endurance 45 s-8 min ES 0.40 (0.27-0.54); muscular endurance ES 0.37 (0.15-0.59) - reps to failure across multiple sets at 80% 1RM; Yo-Yo Intermittent Recovery Test ES 0.36 (0.10-0.63) MODERATE GRADE; 2000 m rowing mean power +1.4% (0.1-2.6); multi-day loading Wingate peak power ES 1.21 and mean power ES 1.26 (largest in literature but only 3 studies, publication bias strongly suspected). de Oliveira 2022 comprehensive SR&MA of 158 SB studies: pooled ES 0.17 (95% CrI 0.12-0.21), mean [HCO3-] rise +5.2 mmol/L, greatest benefit efforts 0.5-10 min. Miller 2025 ITT + trim-and-fill continuous running meta (n=126, 11 RCTs): adjusted SMD 0.18 (-0.01 to 0.36, p=0.06) negligible in mixed-sex pool; male-only subgroup SMD 0.40 significant; GI symptoms 29.5% vs 2.6% placebo; GI withdrawal 8.7% vs 1.6%. Part of effect is placebo (ISSN position stand acknowledges directly).',
