    short_description: 'Connective tissue ADAPTATION slot - NOT a protein entry. Whey Protein doctrine unamended (DIAAS 0, no leucine trigger, does NOT count toward daily protein target). Best-evidenced use in library after creatine for connective tissue, though the aggregate GRADE certainty is LOW to VERY LOW. Load does the work; collagen modifies an adaptation loading creates. AIS Group B (emerging). Dose has moved from the classic 15g convention to 20-30g per Nulty 2024 and AIS position.',
    what_it_does: 'Collagen is the dominant structural protein of the extracellular matrix - most abundant protein in the body, resides in skin, bone, ligaments and tendons, triple-helical structure produces rigid durable tissue. Type I (tendon, ligament, bone matrix, skin) is the primary target of this entry. Glycine occupies every third residue of the helix; collagen preparations run ~24-27.5g glycine and 13-16g proline per 100g protein against only ~3-4g leucine - the amino acid signature that makes collagen excellent for matrix and useless for myofibrillar synthesis. Three mechanistic strands of unequal strength: (a) SUBSTRATE PROVISION - solid, ingestion produces a large transient rise in the exact amino acids the helix is built from with peak at 40-60 min post-ingestion per AIS; underpinned by Melendez-Hevia deficit modelling (~10g/day glycine shortfall in a 70kg adult due to serine hydroxymethyltransferase stoichiometric cap). (b) PEPTIDE SIGNALLING - plausible but unresolved, hydroxyproline di- and tripeptides survive digestion intact and stimulate fibroblasts in culture but translation to in vivo connective tissue health remains unclear per AIS. (c) VITAMIN C as OBLIGATE COFACTOR - established biochemistry for prolyl hydroxylase and lysyl hydroxylase (deficiency = scurvy). Foundational trials: Shaw 2017 AJCN (Australian AIS-funded, 15g vit-C-enriched gelatin 1h pre 6 min rope skipping, engineered ligaments doubled PINP - the origin trial); Alcock 2019 (gelatin vs hydrolysed equivalent plasma AA availability); Lis & Baar 2019 (replication softer - did NOT reach significance); Praet 2019 (TENDOFORTE 5g/day pilot Achilles tendinopathy, VISA-A +12.6 vs MCID 6.5). Modern tendon evidence: Jerger 2022 (14 wk resistance, Achilles CSA +11% vs +4.7%); Lee 2023 (30g + 500mg vit C post-session 10 wk, patellar stiffness +18% vs +5.1%); Lee 2024 (30g + 500mg vit C pre-session, professional female soccer, stiffness +15.4% vs +4.6%); Nulty 2024 (dose-response 30g > 15g > 0g PINP AUC). Bischof 2024 SR (19 studies, 768 participants): SMD 0.67 tendon morphology, SMD 0.19 strength - but GRADE VERY LOW for tendon outcomes. Buell 2026 flags critical confound: dose + form + vitamin C are entirely confounded (positive Lee/Nulty studies used 30g + vit C; negative Jerger studies used 5g without vit C) - cannot attribute to dose alone. Aussieker 2023 MSSE: collagen did NOT increase muscle protein synthesis vs whey vs placebo - Whey Protein doctrine intact.',
