      'Tested athletes without HASTA or Informed Sport batch-verified product - Sport Integrity Australia HASTA survey found 35% of 200 AU online sports supplements contained WADA-prohibited substances; strict liability applies regardless of intent',
      'Any client presenting the tingling paraesthesia as evidence of efficacy - paraesthesia is neurosensory (MrgprD receptor activation), NOT proof the supplement is working; misattribution risks over-dosing chase for a bigger tingle',
      'Athletes without prior training-load consideration - AIS explicitly warns beta-alanine may enable higher training intensity during sprint-interval work, raising injury, illness and non-functional overreaching risk. Load management should NOT be relaxed because tolerance has improved',
