        form: 'Leucine-enriched EAA product (LEAA - typically 30-40% leucine, the form used in most older-adult trials per Katsanos 2006) preferred over standard-ratio EAA. Free-form crystalline OR fermented/plant-source (equivalent - source claims are marketing not pharmacology). AU regulatory screen: for domestic sports-performance product, either ARTG-listed medicine (AUST L number displayed) OR imported. Non-compliant domestic supply is likely a material proportion of the market given S29-18 gap - screen accordingly. HASTA or Informed Sport batch-tested for any tested athlete verified in Sport Integrity app. NOT peptide-bound "EAA" products (rice-derived hydrolysates) as substitute where absorption is clinical reason - different product requiring peptidase activity. Sourcing note for values-sensitive clients: AIS notes purified amino acids commonly derived from animal feathers/fur/hair/skin, plant proteins, or GMO fermentation - source frequently not disclosed. Direct religious/ethical/vegan clients to products explicitly declaring fermentation-derived or plant-derived amino acids.',
        dose: '**3-6 g leucine-enriched EAA per dose** for older-adult appetite-limited scenario (matches sarcopenia RCT dose range 3-6 g/day per Rondanelli 2018, Kim 2012, Tokuda 2021 in Xie 2026); **6-10 g EAA** for fasted-training scenario. EAA intake counted WITHIN total protein target NOT added on top - a 10 g EAA serve is roughly the EAA equivalent of 23-25 g whey. Marketing doses of 6-15 g are NOT evidence-derived; sit between sarcopenia trial doses (3-6 g/day) and acute MPS mechanistic doses (1.5-18 g per bolus) and derive from neither.',
        timing: 'Older-adult appetite-limited: 2-3 distributed doses per day BETWEEN meals so as not to displace food intake (Volpi original rationale: supplements that add energy get compensated for by reduced food intake). Fasted early-morning training: 15-30 min pre-session; whole-protein meal post-session. Long endurance sessions 2h+ with GI-limited whole-protein tolerance: within sports-dietitian-designed fuelling plan. Reduced gastric volume or chewing/swallowing difficulty: distributed alongside APD-led whole-diet strategy.',
